                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "019744b2-06fd-4964-bf87-e4a4fd68d101",
                        "entry_id": "9c45775f-37b3-3cd7-b059-af2a670619a3",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "полага́вшись"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "546b08ba-b6b1-4813-a5af-b42fcc08f7b2",
                        "entry_id": "9c45775f-37b3-3cd7-b059-af2a670619a3",
                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… полага́ться"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b14c2c01-2f1f-3094-85ef-f5aadaa43d31",
                        "entry_id": "9c45775f-37b3-3cd7-b059-af2a670619a3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "доверяться кому-либо или надеяться на что-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8bc10dcd-9a67-4de3-9b00-c47093d7fe34",
                                "sense_id": "b14c2c01-2f1f-3094-85ef-f5aadaa43d31",
                                "text": "Всегда обманутая своим образцом для подражания, всегда рассчитывающая на поддержку, вечно отвергаемая и бессильная, Польша, без сомнения, ожидала французские войска и заранее полагалась на деньги, коими коварная подруга должна ссудить её."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "947dc6e8-f933-3dbd-b688-4d74c3f23d8f",
                        "entry_id": "9c45775f-37b3-3cd7-b059-af2a670619a3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "обычно 3-е лицо причитаться, быть должным"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c72523e-2763-4409-b1b9-88cee4a56bef",
                                "sense_id": "947dc6e8-f933-3dbd-b688-4d74c3f23d8f",
                                "text": "― Пилат протянул слово \"не\" несколько больше, чем это полагается на суде, и послал Иешуа в своём взгляде какую-то мысль, которую как бы хотел внушить арестанту."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d837bad-41e4-4386-9bcd-585212fe5873",
                        "source_entry_id": "9c45775f-37b3-3cd7-b059-af2a670619a3",
                        "source_sense_description": "доверяться, надеяться",
                        "target_lang_word": "rely",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rely",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5e66248-be64-3c79-b7d8-777959c0ae0c",
                                        "entry_id": "766a614c-180d-34ab-8877-908b4bc7a398",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "to trust; to have confidence in; to depend."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "489a2abc-573f-4d27-9187-a19559f83ff6",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e66248-be64-3c79-b7d8-777959c0ae0c",
                                                "text": "I relied on \"George\" and \"Fred\"—the autopilot and the flight director—to fly the airplane while I worked my way through […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "296ab3b3-0de8-48bb-a7a9-82723c6bf0a8",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e66248-be64-3c79-b7d8-777959c0ae0c",
                                                "text": "Cookieless sessions enable you to take advantage of session state without relying on browser cookies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86300e4a-8b90-421d-bdd0-4973f348b1e8",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e66248-be64-3c79-b7d8-777959c0ae0c",
                                                "text": "Shepard: You can't rely on anyone. Sounds harsh, but it's true.\nShepard: It comes down to doing what you think is right--and damn everyone else."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b672393f-118e-4b71-b9c8-a123bf75eb35",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e66248-be64-3c79-b7d8-777959c0ae0c",
                                                "text": "Hodgson also has Wayne Rooney to call on once he has served a two-match suspension at the start of the tournament - and it is abundantly clear England will rely as heavily as ever on his ability to shape the outcome of important games."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e342baf1-ec71-4994-9917-ec7e277a2969",
                                                "sense_id": "d5e66248-be64-3c79-b7d8-777959c0ae0c",
                                                "text": "A “moving platform” scheme[…]is more technologically ambitious than maglev trains even though it relies on conventional rails. Local trains would use side-by-side rails to roll alongside intercity trains and allow passengers to switch trains by stepping through docking bays."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
